var monitor_default = "---\nlayout: article\ntitle: Monitor traffic\ndescription: Use Firewall traffic overview and rule impact preview to understand how Appwrite Firewall handles project requests.\n---\n\nFirewall includes a **traffic overview** on the project Firewall page and an **impact preview** while creating rules. Together they help you validate policies before and after you enable them.\n\n# Traffic overview {% #traffic-overview %}\n\nOpen **Firewall** in your project. Above the rules list, the overview chart and metrics summarize recent traffic for the selected date range and interval.\n\nSeries include:\n\n| Series | Source | Meaning |\n|--------|--------|---------|\n| **Passed** | Project request volume (`network.requests`) | Overall requests in the window (not a Firewall “allowed” counter) |\n| **Denied** | `waf.requests.denied` | Requests rejected by a deny action (`403`) |\n| **Challenged** | `waf.requests.challenged` | Requests challenged by a [challenge action](/docs/products/firewall/actions#challenge) |\n| **Rate limited** | `waf.requests.rateLimited` | Requests throttled over a rate limit quota (`429`) |\n| **Redirected** | `waf.requests.redirected` | Requests answered with a redirect action |\n\n{% info title=\"What is not counted\" %}\n**Bypass** matches and under-quota **rate limit** matches do not publish a Firewall outcome metric. They allow the request and stop further rule evaluation without incrementing denied or rate-limited series.\n{% /info %}\n\nUse the date range picker and interval controls to zoom into an incident window or review longer trends. Refresh to load the latest available data for your plan's usage retention.\n\n# Reading the metrics {% #reading-the-metrics %}\n\n- A spike in **Denied** after creating a path deny rule usually means the rule is matching API (or edge) traffic. Confirm the path is intentional if legitimate clients are affected.\n- **Rate limited** rising with traffic load suggests the per-IP quota is engaged; raise the limit, lengthen the interval, or narrow conditions if false positives appear.\n- High **Passed** with flat denied can mean rules are disabled, priorities favor bypass, conditions do not match real traffic, or you are only browsing in the Console (which Firewall does not block).\n\nCompare overview trends with the rules list (enabled state, priority, and action) on the same page.\n\n# Impact preview {% #impact-preview %}\n\nWhen you [create a rule](/docs/products/firewall/create), the wizard sidebar estimates how many recent usage events would match your current conditions for the selected resource scope and date range.\n\nUse impact preview to:\n\n- Catch overly broad path or country filters before enabling deny\n- Size rate limit quotas against observed request volume\n- Validate that an IP allowlist matches the traffic you expect (single IPs or CIDR ranges)\n\nImpact is an estimate from recent events, not a guarantee of future volume.\n\n# Related debugging {% #related-debugging %}\n\nProject usage dashboards and product logs remain available for deeper debugging. Firewall overview focuses on request volume plus Firewall decision metrics.\n\nWhen testing rules, use a client SDK or API key. Firewall does not block Console access.\n\n{% arrow_link href=\"/docs/products/firewall/update\" %}\nUpdate a rule\n{% /arrow_link %}\n";
export { monitor_default as default };
